          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Without using any tools, write eight full sentences, each about 30 words long, about how rivers shape valleys over time. Plain prose, one paragraph.",
            "text_elements": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "threadId": "01a1601c-37b8-7350-9d43-bf657659a475",
      "turnId": "01a1601c-3830-7cc0-bdc2-a9887f1d1fc2",
      "completedAtMs": 1792613827304
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "item/completed",
    "payload": {
      "item": {
        "type": "reasoning",
        "id": "rs_0ea6d27bb060c75b016ad91dc4c58c81919cb8749035eb9b50",
        "summary": [],
        "content": []
      },
      "threadId": "01a1601c-37b8-7350-9d43-bf657659a475",
      "turnId": "01a1601c-3830-7cc0-bdc2-a9887f1d1fc2",
      "completedAtMs": 1792613828797
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_0ea6d27bb060c75b016ad91dc4cde88191884ba4ef19c3b4e5",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": "Rivers gradually carve valleys as flowing water erodes soil, gravel, and bedrock, deepening channels and creating pathways through landscapes that may initially appear solid and unchanging."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_0ea6d27bb060c75b016ad91dc4cde88191884ba4ef19c3b4e5",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " During floods, rivers spread across their banks, depositing layers of sediment that build fertile floodplains and widen valley floors while continually reshaping surrounding terrain."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_0ea6d27bb060c75b016ad91dc4cde88191884ba4ef19c3b4e5",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " In mountainous regions, swift currents cut narrow, steep-sided gorges, especially where resistant rock forces water to concentrate its energy within confined channels."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_0ea6d27bb060c75b016ad91dc4cde88191884ba4ef19c3b4e5",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " Downstream, gentler slopes reduce water velocity, allowing rivers to meander, erode outer banks, deposit sediment inside bends, and create broad, winding valleys over centuries."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_0ea6d27bb060c75b016ad91dc4cde88191884ba4ef19c3b4e5",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " Tributaries join larger rivers, extending erosion into neighboring hillsides and producing branching drainage patterns that gradually organize entire watersheds across continents."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_0ea6d27bb060c75b016ad91dc4cde88191884ba4ef19c3b4e5",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " Seasonal changes in rainfall and snowmelt alter river power, causing alternating periods of incision, sediment accumulation, bank collapse, and renewed channel migration throughout valley systems."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_0ea6d27bb060c75b016ad91dc4cde88191884ba4ef19c3b4e5",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " Vegetation stabilizes some banks by anchoring soil with roots, yet rivers can undermine those roots, topple trees, and redirect channels during powerful storms."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_0ea6d27bb060c75b016ad91dc4cde88191884ba4ef19c3b4e5",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " Over immense spans of time, these combined processes transform rugged highlands into layered valleys, connecting uplands, plains, ecosystems, and human communities along flowing corridors."
    }
  },
